# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / tooling state — never tracked, never shipped.
#
# .workbuddy/ holds this project's working memory (.workbuddy/memory/*.md).
# It appears at the repo root AND nested inside an example
# (examples/<Name>/.workbuddy/), so the pattern is deliberately unanchored:
# a leading slash would only match the root one and the nested copy — which
# holds an agent's notes for that example, complete with absolute paths —
# would be committed.  tools/package_release.py excludes the same names from
# the release archive; preflight.py asserts neither ever reaches a zip.
#
# .freebuff/ is another harness's project state (just a project-id file), but
# it is the same category and has no business in the published tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.workbuddy/
.freebuff/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — regenerate with `python tools/package_release.py`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default build output of `build_from_spec.py` (its --out defaults to
# <repo>/squareline).  The real examples keep their projects under
# examples/<Name>/squareline/<Name>/, which is NOT ignored — only this
# top-level scratch build is.  package_release.py excludes it from SHIP_TOP.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/squareline/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SquareLine editor churn — created on save inside a project directory.
# tools/package_release.py and eval/run_regression.py ignore the same names.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/squareline/*/backup/
**/squareline/*/cache/
**/squareline/*/components/
**/squareline/*/ui/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated previews — the tool re-creates them on demand.
# NB: examples/*/mockup*.html are Stage-B *deliverables*; do not ignore those.
# examples/<Name>/preview_*/ is a curated deliverable directory too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/preview_from_project.html
**/*.spec_preview.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch.  An underscore-prefixed basename is a throwaway the author
# never intended to keep (tools/_audit.html, tools/_icon_audit.png,
# tools/_proj_preview.html).  Nothing legitimate uses the prefix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
